From 1c37d29a6d85438d5c06f72b336a31ac63e5cf2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Coinupbtc <coinupbtc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:11:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] lane host: read a finished reply ahead while the client
 runs its tools (TF_DS_STEP_AHEAD=1)

An agent's next request is its last prompt, the reply and the tool results, but the prompt cache keeps states only at a prompt
pass's chunk ends, so that request resumed at its previous prompt's last kept chunk end and read its own previous reply
again. With TF_DS_STEP_AHEAD=1, when a reply ends and nothing else runs or waits, rank 0 queues a background prompt pass of
prompt + reply, cut at the last chunk end of the family's grid that leaves its tail, and keeps a state there; it runs
while the client runs its tools. Up to that point the pass is the next request's own cold pass: the same grid and tokens.

By Coinupbtc (pull request #41, rebased as #66 by Braincramps onto 0001-0029), carried onto this series after the prompt
steps (0037): a request that continues a step-ahead pass that is mid-way waits for its state (admitOne), instead of
reading the same tokens itself, and a request that does not continue it cancels it (submit); a step-ahead pass is not
requeued when the pool is full. Host tests (the step-ahead tests also run with prompts read a chunk a turn), and a
stepped test of both arrivals: without the wait the arrival resumes at 4 instead of 12.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
